    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0180" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg168"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.60c/68: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-04-17T22:00:00+01:00">April 17, 1939—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 17—4:31 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>505. The Foreign Office informs me that the British Ambassador at Warsaw has been
                    advised by Beck<anchor n="64" xml:id="d167-f1"/> that he was authorized to state
                    Great Britain can count on the assistance of Poland if she is involved in a war
                    with Germany by reason of an attack made on any of the <pb facs="0181" n="169"
                        xml:id="pg169"/> smaller western European countries such as Belgium or
                    Holland. At Beck’s request this communication is not to be made public.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d167-f1" n="64" xml:id="d167-f1-content">
                <p>Józef Beck, Polish Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
